 "notes": "The horseshoe reef of Sha'ab Samadai opening to the south: the lagoon (Zone A for the dolphins only, Zone B for snorkelling), and the diving area Zone C with the boat moorings, the maze of pinnacles, the caves and canyons south-west of the lagoon mouth, the drop-off to 40 m on the west and sand to 25 m in the south. Reef outline and pinnacles from OpenStreetMap (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL); the zones follow the HEPCA zoning as described on the web. The zone boundaries and the mooring position are schematic; the route runs through the cave system first, then the canyons. All positions are approximate.",
